rs to stay connected, navigate safely, enhance operational efficiency, and ensure crew welfare. Inmarsat Maritime is based in Viasat’s global international business headquarters in London, United Kingdom.", "VIASAT:Viasat is a global communications company that believes everyone and everything in the world can be connected. With offices in 24 countries, Viasat is developing a global communications network to provide high-quality, reliable, secure, affordable, and fast connections. In May 2023, Viasat completed its acquisition of Inmarsat, combining the teams, technologies, and resources of the two companies to create a new global communications partner.", "NEXUSWAVE:NexusWave is a new bonded network service launched by Inmarsat Maritime in May 2023. It integrates multiple high-speed networks in real time to enable high-speed, always-on ship-to-shore communications. NexusWave offers high-speed connectivity, unlimited data, global coverage, and secure infrastructure for office-like and home-like experiences. It integrates Global Xpress (GX) Ka-band, low-Earth orbit (LEO) services, and coastal LTE service, enhanced by an L-band layer for resiliency.", "AKIHIRO FUJIMARU:Akihiro Fujimaru is the Managing Executive Officer of \"K\" LINE. He has emphasized the importance of fast, reliable, and global connectivity services for enhancing safety, quality, and the well-being of the crew, as well as supporting digitalization initiatives and automated ship navigation.", "BEN PALMER:Ben Palmer OBE is the President of Inmarsat Maritime. He has expressed honor in partnering with \"K\" LINE to trial NexusWave on its fleet, highlighting the strategic foresight of \"K\" LINE’s commitment to leveraging advanced technology for operational success and competitive edge.", "YUKIKAZU MYOCHIN:Yukikazu Myochin is the President & CEO of \"K\" LINE. He is involved in the partnership with Inmarsat Maritime for the trial of NexusWave on \"K\" LINE's fleet.", "GLOBAL XPRESS (GX) KA-BAND:Global Xpress (GX) Ka-band is a high-speed connectivity service integrated into NexusWave, providing reliable global coverage for ship-to-shore communications.", "LOW-EARTH ORBIT (LEO) SERVICES:Low-Earth orbit (LEO) services are part of the NexusWave network, offering enhanced connectivity for maritime communications.", "COASTAL LTE SERVICE:Coastal LTE service is an as-available connectivity option integrated into NexusWave, providing additional resiliency for maritime communications.", "L-BAND LAYER:The L-band layer is an enhancement in the NexusWave network, providing additional resiliency for high-speed, always-on connectivity.", "VIASAT-3 KA-BAND SATELLITES:The ViaSat-3 Ka-band satellites are high-capacity satellites anticipated to launch, which will bolster the digitalization initiatives and connectivity services provided by NexusWave.", "KAWASAKI KISEN KAISHA, LTD.:", "VIASAT-3:The ViaSat-3 class satellites are a series of satellites that are anticipated to provide significant benefits and are part of future satellite construction or acquisition plans"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}